# ember

A read-only alert reporter for a single server. Ember polls host and Docker
metrics, evaluates threshold alerts, has an LLM agent triage what fired (using
read-only shell/filesystem tools), and sends a structured report to your
sinks. Nothing listens for replies — every sink is one-way.

Ember also polls configured RSS/Atom feeds independently of metric alerts.
New entries go directly to the agent for a summary and then to every enabled
sink, using the same structured report format.

## Sinks

- **discord** — webhook. Create one in your notification channel
  (Settings → Integrations → Webhooks) and set `[discord] webhook_url`.
  Reports arrive as embeds, color-coded by severity.
- **email** — plain SMTP, STARTTLS by default (`[email]` section).
- slack / telegram — not implemented; toggles are reserved in `[sinks]`.

## Configuration

Copy `config.example.toml` to `config.toml` in the repo root and fill it in.
Secrets live only in `config.toml`, which is gitignored.

### RSS / Atom

Configure feed URLs under `[rss]`, for example Ubuntu security notices:

```toml
[rss]
feeds = ["https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/rss.xml"]
interval = 900
send_existing = false
```

An empty list (or no `[rss]` section) disables feed polling. The interval is in
seconds and independent of metric collection. The first successful fetch of
each new feed establishes a baseline without reporting historical entries;
set `send_existing = true` to report the current backlog instead. Later entries
are deduplicated by feed URL and entry ID (falling back to link or content hash).
Edits to an already-seen ID do not generate a new report.

State lives in `data/rss.sqlite3` (`rss.state_path` to override); Compose keeps
it in the `ember-data` volume. Keep this state across restarts to avoid replay
or re-baselining. Feed failures are isolated and retried next cycle. Reports
contain up to `rss.batch_size` entries (default/max 10); `rss.timeout` defaults
to 30 seconds. Failed deliveries are retried while the entries remain in the
feed; successful sinks can receive duplicates if another sink fails or the
process stops between delivery and saving state. If the model fails, a raw
informational report with source links is sent instead.

Feed content is untrusted. The agent is instructed to summarize it, not obey
embedded instructions, and never to apply updates itself.

The RSS-specific instructions live in `config/defaults/prompts/rss.md` and can
be overridden with `config/prompts/rss.md`, like the triage prompt.

### Prompts

The agent's instructions are every `*.md` file in `config/prompts/` plus
`config/defaults/prompts/`, concatenated in sorted filename order — no
filenames are hardcoded. A file in `config/prompts/` (gitignored) overrides
the same-named default wholesale; nothing is copied or merged at startup, so
`git pull` can never overwrite your customizations.

`config/defaults/prompts/triage.md` is the out-of-the-box triage prompt;
override it by creating your own `config/prompts/triage.md`, or add new
`*.md` files alongside it.

## Run

    docker compose up -d --build

or locally:

    uv run python main.py

The container mounts the Docker socket (metrics), `/` at `/host` read-only
(agent filesystem tools), and `config.toml` / `config/prompts` read-only from
the host.

## Tests

    uv run python -m unittest discover -s tests -v

Tests use mocked HTTP, agent, and sink calls; no API keys or live deliveries
are needed.
